UID:10010156-1775380500-1775384100@faithatfirst.org
SUMMARY:Abide
DESCRIPTION:Sundays at 9:15am in Room K. \nAbide provides ongoing space for spiritual connection to God\, mutual support in community\, and faith formation in the ways that lead to life. This gathering is open to all who seek to abide with Jesus through the Spirit in the company of friends. \nAbide meets Sunday mornings at 9:15am in person.  New participants are always welcome. \nFacilitator:  Mari Leonard\, mari.leonard@comcast.net \nRealm Registration Event. 
URL:https://faithatfirst.org/event/abide-3/2026-04-05/
LOCATION:Room K
ORGANIZER;CN="Mari Leonard":MAILTO:mari.leonard@comcast.net
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260405T091500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260405T101500
DTSTAMP:20260401T203225
CREATED:20250905T023024Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20250905T023024Z
UID:10010246-1775380500-1775384100@faithatfirst.org
SUMMARY:The Christian Experiment
DESCRIPTION:Sundays at 9:15am in Glenna Hall Sundays\, first floor. Begins Sept. 14.\nThe Christian Experiment is a weekly gathering that creates community and explores faith-based questions. Ever had doubts? If you are like most\, you have. Ever had doubts about Christian faith? Many of us have. In a recent study at a leading United Methodist Church\, 95 percent of believers stated they struggle with doubt occasionally and 24 percent stated they struggle with doubt regularly. This same study also found that 44 percent believed their doubts helped them find or strengthen their faith.\nFacilitators:   Matt Rader (mrader@emich.edu) and Kristi Hubbard (hubbard.kristi@gmail.com) \nRealm Registration Event. 
URL:https://faithatfirst.org/event/the-christian-experiment-2/2026-04-05/
LOCATION:Glenna Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260405T091500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260405T101500
DTSTAMP:20260401T203225
CREATED:20250905T023256Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20250905T151229Z
UID:10010283-1775380500-1775384100@faithatfirst.org
SUMMARY:History\, Roots\, & Rearview Mirror
DESCRIPTION:History\, Roots and a Rearview Mirror will use insight and discussion to understand our roots and history to have a rearview mirror of our story. The class will begin with a two-week unit on First Church history; followed by a four-week unit on church history under Constantine; a two-week unit on history of human sexuality in the UMC; a two-week unit on the history of race and racism in the UMC; and finish the year on Advent with the Wesleys. \nRealm Registration Event. 
URL:https://faithatfirst.org/event/history-roots-rearview-mirror/2026-04-05/
LOCATION:Conference Room
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260405T091500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260405T101500
DTSTAMP:20260401T203225
CREATED:20250905T152139Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20250905T152217Z
UID:10010332-1775380500-1775384100@faithatfirst.org
SUMMARY:Confirmation Class
DESCRIPTION:Sundays 9:15-10:15am (7-8th Grade) \nConfirmation is the culmination of a two-year process that focuses on building relationships with God\, each other\, and the larger faith community. Class meets on Sunday mornings to discuss theology\, spiritual practices\, and living our faith in the world. It’s a time to eat donuts\, for youth to think critically and ask hard questions while growing in love and relationship with God and neighbor. A key focus is to help youth develop a sense of belonging in the congregation. At the conclusion of the process\, 8th graders are invited to take confirmation vows during Sunday worship. \n  \nEmail Sydney@faithatfirst.com with questions!
URL:https://faithatfirst.org/event/confirmation-class-30/2026-04-05/
LOCATION:Youth Room
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260405T091500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260405T101500
DTSTAMP:20260401T203225
CREATED:20251002T170240Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251002T170240Z
UID:10011036-1775380500-1775384100@faithatfirst.org
SUMMARY:Sunday Morning Book Club
DESCRIPTION:Sunday Morning Book Club- Sundays at 9:15am- Begins Oct. 5th\n\nBegins October 5th in Room 32. \nSunday Morning Book Club is multigenerational group of adults integrating learning and faith through secular or biblical stories. Reading the book is great but is not required. For questions or more information\, please contact the class leaders. \nThe first book seletced is The Anxious Generation by Jonatahn Haidt and is discussed 10/5 – 11/16. \nDiscussion leaders are Matt Peters (Matthew.mjp.peters@gmail.com) and Julie Womack (womackjulie@gmail.com)
URL:https://faithatfirst.org/event/sunday-morning-book-club/2026-04-05/
LOCATION:Room 32
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260405T091500
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260405T101500
DTSTAMP:20260401T203225
CREATED:20260319T155620Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260319T155620Z
UID:10011720-1775380500-1775384100@faithatfirst.org
SUMMARY:Social Justice Intersections - One Church One Book
DESCRIPTION:Wesleyan Vile-tality\n\nSJI launches a four-week study of FUMC’s One Church/One Book\, “Wesleyan Vile-tality: Reclaiming the Heart of Methodist Identity.” It was written by Dr. Ashley Boggan\, who led SJI and preached here last Fall. Boggan argues that the early Methodists\, following the lead of John and Charles Wesley\, were considered vile. They were “rule-benders\, rabble-rousers\, and outcast-embracers.” Somewhere along the way\, Methodists chose to become respectable. Boggan calls us to return to our original vile-tality as we address racism\, sexism\, heterosexism\, and colonialism. Books are available at the church office for $10.\n\nDiscussion facilitators are:\n\nMarch 8: The Call to Wesleyan Vile-tality – Chapters 1 and 2 – Martha Rudy\n\nMarch 15: Losing Vile-tality – Chapter 3 – Matt Moy Johnson\n\nMarch 22: Vile Sustainers – Chapter 4 – Tom Scott\n\nMarch 29: Reclaiming Vile-tality – Chapter 5 – Dennis Barbour
URL:https://faithatfirst.org/event/social-justice-intersections-one-church-one-book/2026-04-05/
END:VEVENT
